---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import VeriuboBenchCharts from '../../components/VeriuboBenchCharts.astro';

const lang = 'en' as const;
---

<Base
  lang={lang}
  title="VeriUBO — Shaw X"
  description="An AI corporate due-diligence workbench — nine FATF gates, cyclic ownership math, OFAC 50% Rule, and a zero-leak client portal."
>
  <Nav lang={lang} />
  <main class="container case">
    <a class="back mono" href="/#work">← Selected work</a>

    <header class="head">
      <h1>VeriUBO</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        An AI corporate due-diligence workbench for bank onboarding — nine FATF gates,
        cyclic ownership math, OFAC 50% Rule, and a zero-leak client portal.
      </p>
      <a class="try-live" href="https://github.com/shawx001/VeriUBO" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        View on GitHub <span class="tl-arrow">↗</span>
      </a>
    </header>

    <div class="meta">
      <div class="meta-item">
        <span class="meta-label mono">Context</span>
        <span class="meta-value">Independent product<br />2026 · v2.1 shipped</span>
      </div>
      <div class="meta-item">
        <span class="meta-label mono">My role</span>
        <span class="meta-value">Creator — product,<br />design, architecture</span>
      </div>
      <div class="meta-item">
        <span class="meta-label mono">Status</span>
        <span class="meta-value">Open-source prototype<br />local LLM + live data</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="shot dark">
      <figure class="screen-frame">
        <img
          src="/case/veriubo/dossier.png"
          alt="VeriUBO Executive Legal Binder workspace showing the nine FATF due-diligence gates on the left, live OFAC sanctions review in the center, and rationale contradiction guardrails"
          width="1440"
          height="900"
        />
      </figure>
      <p class="shot-cap mono">executive legal binder — nine FATF gates, calm triage, live sanctions review</p>
    </div>

    <section class="block">
      <p class="b-label mono">01 — Overview</p>
      <h2>The AI investigates. The rules engine decides.</h2>
      <p>
        Corporate bank onboarding (KYB) has zero room for hand-waving: who actually owns
        the company through layered or circular holdings, whether a sanctions alias is a
        real hit or a namesake, and what happens if registry details shift after sign-off.
        VeriUBO puts a local agent on intake triage and follow-up while keeping every
        ownership solver, expiry rule, and approval gate deterministic on the server.
      </p>
      <p>
        In the flagship case, merging <strong>James Chen</strong> (12.5%) and
        <strong>J. Chen</strong> (14%) crosses the 25% beneficial-owner threshold at
        <strong>26.5%</strong> and automatically inserts him into the required identity
        roster. Clearing his simulated sanctions alias does not satisfy personal identity
        verification — senior sign-off still returns <strong>HTTP 409</strong> until an
        independent ID record is filed.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <p class="b-label mono">02 — How it works</p>
      <h2>Three personas. One deterministic spine.</h2>
      <div
        class="pipeline"
        role="img"
        aria-label="Workflow: Client Portal submits sanitized documents, Deterministic Engine and Background Agent solve ownership and screen sanctions, Analyst and Independent Senior Approver verify and sign off"
      >
        <div class="p-flow">
          <div class="p-step">
            <span class="p-name mono">Client Portal</span>
            <span class="p-desc">sanitized self-service intake for business profile, filings and IDs</span>
          </div>
          <span class="p-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          <div class="p-step p-core">
            <span class="p-name mono">Engine + Agent</span>
            <span class="p-desc">Leontief UBO solver, OFAC 50% Rule, GLEIF LEI &amp; proactive triage</span>
          </div>
          <span class="p-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          <div class="p-step">
            <span class="p-name mono">Analyst &amp; Approver</span>
            <span class="p-desc">legal-binder dossier, four-eyes sign-off &amp; versioned audit export</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="p-gate mono">when registry records change after approval — the case automatically reopens</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <p class="b-label mono">03 — Three roles, three views</p>
      <h2>Same case. Each role sees only its part.</h2>
      <div class="roles">
        <figure class="role">
          <a class="role-shot" href="/case/veriubo/role-analyst.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            <img src="/case/veriubo/role-analyst.png" alt="Case analyst view: prioritised due-diligence queue with blockers and the suggested next step for each case" width="1024" height="728" loading="lazy" />
          </a>
          <figcaption>
            <span class="role-tag mono">Case analyst</span>
            <h3>Works the queue</h3>
            <p>Prioritised cases, open blockers, and the next step the agent suggests. Investigates, resolves name matches, and submits for approval.</p>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="role">
          <a class="role-shot" href="/case/veriubo/role-approver.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            <img src="/case/veriubo/role-approver.png" alt="Independent senior approver view: sign-off dialog with the nine-check snapshot, approve, escalate and reject decisions, and the server-side block notice" width="1024" height="640" loading="lazy" />
          </a>
          <figcaption>
            <span class="role-tag mono">Senior approver</span>
            <h3>Signs off, independently</h3>
            <p>Decides against a frozen snapshot of one case version. The server rejects sign-off by the same person who worked the case.</p>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="role">
          <a class="role-shot" href="/case/veriubo/role-client.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            <img src="/case/veriubo/role-client.png" alt="Client portal view: list of missing documents with automatic pre-checks and submission receipts, no internal risk data shown" width="1024" height="728" loading="lazy" />
          </a>
          <figcaption>
            <span class="role-tag mono">Client</span>
            <h3>Fixes their own gaps</h3>
            <p>Sees only the documents still missing and why a file failed its pre-check. No sanctions hits, risk ratings or analyst notes.</p>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <p class="b-label mono">04 — Key capabilities</p>
      <h2>Four things built for real audits.</h2>

      <div class="feature">
        <div class="f-text">
          <h3>Cyclic ownership forensics</h3>
          <p>
            Nested cross-holdings break naive recursive scripts. A unified three-column
            workspace pairs original PDF bounding boxes and 300 DPI crops on the left,
            a Leontief linear-algebra equity graph in the middle, and human-in-the-loop
            homonym resolution on the right — recomputing required UBOs the moment
            aliases merge.
          </p>
        </div>
        <figure class="f-visual screen-card">
          <img
            src="/case/veriubo/ownership.png"
            alt="Three-column Multimodal Ownership Forensics view with PDF bounding boxes on the left, interactive Leontief ownership graph in the center, and homonym collision entity merger on the right"
            width="1440"
            height="900"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </figure>
      </div>

      <div class="feature flip">
        <div class="f-text">
          <h3>OFAC 50% Rule, done straight</h3>
          <p>
            Under OFAC FAQ 401, economic ownership and blocked control are not the same
            number. If a sanctioned person owns 50% of a holding company that owns 50% of
            the applicant, effective economic equity is 25% — yet cascading blocked control
            reaches 50%, triggering an automatic block. VeriUBO computes and displays both
            metrics side by side.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="f-visual">
          <div class="receipt">
            <p class="r-title mono">OFAC FAQ 401 · dual-metric check</p>
            <div class="r-row">
              <span>Sanctioned party → HoldCo</span>
              <span class="mono">50.0%</span>
            </div>
            <div class="r-row">
              <span>HoldCo → Applicant</span>
              <span class="mono">50.0%</span>
            </div>
            <div class="r-row">
              <span>Deduplicated economic equity</span>
              <span class="mono">25.0%</span>
            </div>
            <div class="r-row accent">
              <span>Cascading OFAC blocked control</span>
              <span class="mono">50.0% · BLOCKED</span>
            </div>
            <p class="r-cap mono">screened locally against 19,629 live OFAC SDN records</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="feature">
        <div class="f-text">
          <h3>Zero-leak client self-service</h3>
          <p>
            Analysts lose days chasing missing files over email, yet you can never expose
            internal sanctions hits or risk flags to an applicant. Switching to the client
            portal serves strictly sanitized document requests and structured business
            profile inputs — routing every upload straight back into the analyst's queue.
          </p>
        </div>
        <figure class="f-visual screen-card">
          <img
            src="/case/veriubo/client-portal.png"
            alt="Zero-leak Client Self-Service Portal allowing applicants to submit business profile information and missing KYC documents without seeing internal compliance alerts"
            width="1440"
            height="900"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </figure>
      </div>

      <div class="feature flip">
        <div class="f-text">
          <h3>Four-eyes sign-off &amp; contradiction guards</h3>
          <p>
            Senior approval rejects self-review on the server. Switching a sanctions
            disposition or approval verdict clears stale text and enforces a consistent
            rationale — preventing an exported audit bundle from recording a rejection
            alongside an escalation memo.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="f-visual">
          <div class="escalate">
            <p class="fc-head mono">server gate · HTTP 409 conflict</p>
            <p class="e-line">
              Required UBO <strong>James Chen (26.5%)</strong> lacks independent identity
              verification, and senior sign-off requires an approver distinct from the
              case analyst.
            </p>
            <div class="e-chips">
              <span class="e-chip mono">Approval blocked · 409</span>
              <span class="e-chip muted mono">Four-eyes enforced</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <p class="b-label mono">05 — Post-training &amp; eval design</p>
      <h2>Built for one 16 GB GPU — calibrated to abstain when unsure.</h2>
      <p>
        Zero-shot vision models struggle on degraded corporate scans: smudged
        <code>0/O</code> and <code>3/8</code> digits, cross-page table shifts, silent
        fabrication, and reckless homonym merges. Rather than shipping private KYC filings
        to cloud APIs, VeriUBO specifies a four-stage on-prem post-training pipeline sized
        for a single <strong>RTX 5080 (16 GB)</strong> — keeping live local inference
        within <strong>12.5 GB VRAM</strong>.
      </p>

      <div class="pt-grid">
        <div class="pt-card">
          <span class="g-num mono">Stage 01 · &lt; 6 GB VRAM</span>
          <h3>PP-OCRv4 Rec-only fine-tune</h3>
          <p>Freeze the detector; tune the recognition tail and CTC/NRTR heads on degraded crops (stamp overlap, skew, blur), exposing per-character Shannon entropy to trigger 300 DPI zoom.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pt-card">
          <span class="g-num mono">Stage 02 · 4-bit NF4</span>
          <h3>Qwen2.5-VL-7B QLoRA SFT</h3>
          <p>4-bit NF4 base with <code>bf16</code> compute and assistant-token loss masking on multi-turn grounded bounding-box extraction and <code>crop_and_inspect(dpi=300)</code> tool traces.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pt-card">
          <span class="g-num mono">Stage 03 · RL Alignment</span>
          <h3>Verifier-guided Asymmetric-Risk DPO</h3>
          <p>Mine hard negatives from symbolic Leontief violations, penalizing silent fabrication and homonym false-merges far more heavily than conservative deferral; includes a <code>verl</code> GRPO reward hook.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pt-card">
          <span class="g-num mono">Stage 04 · Calibration</span>
          <h3>Conformal Risk Control gate</h3>
          <p>Calibrate straight-through processing (STP) under an explicit mis-merge risk cap <code>α ≤ 1%</code>, routing uncertain graphs to analyst review instead of silently passing.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <VeriuboBenchCharts lang={lang} />

      <div class="bench-card">
        <div class="bench-head">
          <div>
            <p class="r-title mono">UBO-Bench v1.0 · Ablation comparison</p>
            <p class="bench-sub mono">240 zero-leakage synthetic holdout (Customer × Template split) + 40 public OOD (22 UKCH · 18 SEC EDGAR)</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="table-wrap">
          <table class="bench-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Stage / Variant</th>
                <th class="num">Ownership F1</th>
                <th class="num">UBO Recall</th>
                <th class="num">Mis-Merge</th>
                <th class="num">STP @ 1% cap</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td>Qwen2.5-VL-7B (Zero-Shot) <span class="v-tag mono">Baseline</span></td>
                <td class="num mono">0.71</td>
                <td class="num mono">0.74</td>
                <td class="num mono">4.80%</td>
                <td class="num mono">34.0%</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Base PP-OCRv4 + Qwen2.5-VL-7B LoRA SFT <span class="v-tag mono">+ SFT</span></td>
                <td class="num mono">0.79</td>
                <td class="num mono">0.83</td>
                <td class="num mono">2.60%</td>
                <td class="num mono">52.0%</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>FT PP-OCRv4 (Rec-only) + QLoRA SFT <span class="v-tag mono">+ OCR FT</span></td>
                <td class="num mono">0.84</td>
                <td class="num mono">0.87</td>
                <td class="num mono">1.90%</td>
                <td class="num mono">59.5%</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>+ Active 300 DPI Zoom + Leontief Verifier <span class="v-tag mono">+ Symbolic</span></td>
                <td class="num mono">0.89</td>
                <td class="num mono">0.94</td>
                <td class="num mono">1.30%</td>
                <td class="num mono">66.0%</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="hi">
                <td>VeriUBO Full (+ Asymmetric-Risk DPO + Conformal Gate) <span class="v-tag mono">16GB Target</span></td>
                <td class="num mono">0.92</td>
                <td class="num mono">0.97</td>
                <td class="num mono">0.82%</td>
                <td class="num mono">73.5%</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="ref">
                <td>GPT-4o + Symbolic Verifier <span class="v-tag mono">Cloud Ref</span></td>
                <td class="num mono">0.88</td>
                <td class="num mono">0.93</td>
                <td class="num mono">1.40%</td>
                <td class="num mono">64.5%</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <p class="b-label mono">06 — Measured scope &amp; honest limits</p>
      <h2>What is verified — and where a prototype stops.</h2>
      <div class="goals three">
        <div class="goal">
          <span class="g-num mono">9 / 9 Gates</span>
          <h3>FATF corporate CDD</h3>
          <p>Registry &amp; GLEIF LEI, business profile, filings, ownership graph, signatories, UBO IDs, sanctions, EDD and sign-off.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="goal">
          <span class="g-num mono">19,629 Records</span>
          <h3>Live OFAC SDN + GLEIF</h3>
          <p>Real public OFAC SDN data indexed locally for primary-name and alias screening, alongside live GLEIF LEI verification.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="goal">
          <span class="g-num mono">35 Tool Calls</span>
          <h3>Local LLM replay</h3>
          <p>End-to-end 8-stage lifecycle verified on local Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct, including four-eyes sign-off and registry-change reopen.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="goal">
          <span class="g-num mono">Boundary · 01</span>
          <h3>PEP &amp; adverse media</h3>
          <p>OFAC sanctions screening is live; politically exposed persons and adverse-media research remain analyst-reviewed with citations.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="goal">
          <span class="g-num mono">Boundary · 02</span>
          <h3>Unseen filings OCR</h3>
          <p>Graph math, homonym merges and PDF grounding are verified; raw extraction accuracy on arbitrary unseen foreign registries is not yet benchmarked.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="goal">
          <span class="g-num mono">Boundary · 03</span>
          <h3>Enterprise IAM</h3>
          <p>Local role switching demonstrates four-eyes mechanics; production rollout replaces persona headers with enterprise SSO and live registry feeds.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <p class="tbc"><span class="tbc-dots">…</span>To be continued</p>
  </main>
  <Footer lang={lang} />
</Base>

<style>
  .case { padding: 130px 24px 90px; max-width: 880px; }
  .back {
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    transition: color 0.25s;
  }
  .back:hover { color: var(--accent); }
  .head { margin-top: 34px; }
  .head h1 { font-size: clamp(44px, 7vw, 76px); }
  .lede {
    margin: 18px 0 0;
    font-size: clamp(16px, 2vw, 19px);
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    max-width: 650px;
  }
  .try-live {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5em;
    margin-top: 28px;
    padding: 12px 26px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--accent);
    color: #FFFDF8;
    font-size: 14.5px;
    font-weight: 500;
    transition: transform 0.25s cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1), box-shadow 0.25s;
    box-shadow: 0 14px 30px -14px rgba(216, 90, 48, 0.6);
  }
  .try-live:hover { transform: translateY(-2px); box-shadow: 0 20px 38px -16px rgba(216, 90, 48, 0.7); }
  .tl-arrow { transition: transform 0.25s; }
  .try-live:hover .tl-arrow { transform: translate(2px, -2px); }

  .meta {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 28px;
    margin-top: 52px;
    padding: 28px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }
  .meta-item { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; }
  .meta-label {
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .meta-value { font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink); }

  /* hero screenshot stage */
  .shot {
    margin-top: 56px;
    border-radius: 18px;
    padding: clamp(18px, 3vw, 32px);
    box-shadow: 0 36px 80px -42px rgba(44, 36, 24, 0.55);
  }
  .shot.dark { background: #1A112E; }
  .screen-frame {
    margin: 0;
    border-radius: 11px;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid rgba(245, 239, 228, 0.14);
    background: #120B21;
  }
  .screen-frame img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }
  .shot-cap {
    margin: 18px 0 0;
    text-align: center;
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: rgba(240, 234, 248, 0.52);
  }

  .block { margin-top: 88px; }
  .b-label {
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .block h2 { margin-top: 12px; font-size: clamp(26px, 3.6vw, 38px); }
  .block > p {
    margin: 18px 0 0;
    font-size: 15.5px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--ink);
    max-width: 660px;
  }
  .block > p strong { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; }
  .block code {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.88em;
    background: rgba(44, 36, 24, 0.06);
    padding: 1px 5px;
    border-radius: 5px;
  }

  /* post-training & benchmark design */
  .pt-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 18px;
    margin-top: 30px;
  }
  .pt-card {
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-radius: 14px;
    padding: 22px 22px 20px;
    background: var(--paper, #FFFDF8);
  }
  .pt-card h3 { font-size: 18px; margin-top: 10px; }
  .pt-card p { margin: 8px 0 0; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--ink-2); }

  .bench-card {
    margin-top: 28px;
    background: var(--paper, #FFFDF8);
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-radius: 16px;
    padding: 26px 26px 22px;
    box-shadow: 0 28px 60px -36px rgba(44, 36, 24, 0.42);
  }
  .bench-head {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 16px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }
  .bench-sub {
    margin: 4px 0 0;
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  .status-pill {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    font-size: 10.5px;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
    border: 1px solid var(--accent);
    background: rgba(216, 90, 48, 0.06);
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 5px 12px;
  }
  .table-wrap { overflow-x: auto; }
  .bench-table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 13px;
  }
  .bench-table th {
    text-align: left;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 10.5px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    padding: 10px 8px 10px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .bench-table td {
    padding: 11px 8px 11px 0;
    color: var(--ink);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    vertical-align: middle;
  }
  .bench-table th.num,
  .bench-table td.num {
    text-align: right;
    padding-left: 12px;
    padding-right: 0;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .bench-table tr.hi td {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 600;
    background: rgba(216, 90, 48, 0.05);
  }
  .bench-table tr.hi td:first-child { padding-left: 10px; border-radius: 8px 0 0 8px; }
  .bench-table tr.hi td:last-child { padding-right: 10px; border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0; }
  .bench-table tr.ref td { color: var(--ink-2); border-bottom: none; }
  .v-tag {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-left: 6px;
    font-size: 9.5px;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 1px 7px;
    vertical-align: middle;
  }
  .bench-table tr.hi .v-tag {
    color: var(--accent);
    border-color: rgba(216, 90, 48, 0.45);
  }

  /* pipeline */
  .pipeline {
    margin-top: 28px;
    background: #1A112E;
    border-radius: 18px;
    padding: clamp(24px, 4vw, 44px);
  }
  .p-flow { display: flex; align-items: stretch; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
